# DUPLICATE-LANE NOTE (SP-07/08/09/10 → SP-14):
#   Until SP-14 prunes the migrated lane bodies from ../fastlane/Fastfile, both
#   the legacy file AND the per-target lane.rb files define the same lane
#   symbols (deployReleaseApkOnFirebase, deployDemoApkOnFirebase, deployInternal,
#   promoteToBeta, promote_to_production, deploy_on_firebase, beta, release,
#   plus the lifted :mac block). To avoid Fastlane's duplicate-lane parse
#   error during the migration window, this file imports ONLY the legacy tree
#   today; the per-target imports below are intentionally COMMENTED OUT and
#   will be uncommented + the legacy Fastfile pruned in a single atomic step
#   when SP-14 lands. Until then, `bundle exec fastlane <lane>` continues to
#   resolve lanes from the legacy tree — preserving back-compat exactly per
#   the SP-06 contract.
#
# SP-11 NOTE (release-dispatcher integration — 2026-06-04):
#   The /release {platform} {target} dispatcher (layers/release/commands/release.md
#   "Deployment-tree Dispatch" section) now invokes lanes via
#   `bundle exec fastlane --fastlane-dir deployment <platform> <lane_name>`,
#   making THIS file the canonical entry point. During the SP-11..SP-14 window
#   the per-target imports below remain COMMENTED to avoid duplicate-lane parse
#   errors against the legacy `../fastlane/Fastfile`. The dispatcher's
#   --dry-run default means SP-11 itself does not trigger live lane invocations.
#   SP-14 will atomically: (a) delete ../fastlane/Fastfile lane bodies,
#   (b) uncomment the per-target imports below, (c) remove this paragraph.
